        ecrm:P3_has_note    "British Galleries:\nIn the late Victorian period it was very fashionable to decorate the home with Japanese objects. Textiles such as this, which would have been used in Japan to cover a gift, were particularly popular. The unusual motifs and lavish gold embroidery would have seemed very exotic to the British public. [27/03/2003]"@en ;
